      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Before developing the formal method for inverting a matrix, we consider two extreme (but very useful) cases that lead to simple expressions for the inverse. First, if the matrix is diagonal (all off-diagonal elements are zero), then the matrix inverse is also diagonal, with $ \\mathbf{A}_{ii}^{-1} = 1/A_{ii} $. For example,",
